-- title:
--   Herbrand's theorem in the lower numbering for monogenic DVRs
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a discrete valuation ring which is a domain, let a group $G$ act on $R$ by ring automorphisms, the action being faithful, and let $A$ be a commutative semiring with an $A$-algebra structure on $R$ whose structure map is fixed pointwise by $G$, i.e. $\sigma \cdot \mathrm{alg}_{A\to R}(a) = \mathrm{alg}_{A\to R}(a)$ for all $\sigma \in G$, $a \in A$. Let $H \trianglelefteq G$ be a finite normal subgroup such that the subring $R^H$ of $H$-fixed points is again a discrete valuation ring. Assume: $R$ is generated as an $A$-algebra by a single element $x$ (`Algebra.adjoin A {x} = ⊤`); there is $y \in R^H$ such that every element of $R^H$ lies in the $A$-subalgebra generated by $y$; and the two additive valuations are compatible, $v_R(z) = |H_0| \cdot v_{R^H}(z)$ in $\mathbb{N}_\infty$ for every $z \in R^H$, where $H_0$ is the inertia subgroup of $H$ on $R/\mathfrak{m}_R$, so that $|H_0|$ is [`IsLocalRing.lowerRamificationCard R H 0`](def/Mathlib_RingTheory_Valuation_UpperRamificationGroup.html#L13). Here, for a group $\Gamma$ acting on a local ring $B$, the $n$-th lower ramification group is the inertia subgroup of $\mathfrak{m}_B^{n+1}$ in $\Gamma$, and $\varphi_{\Gamma}(u)$ for $u > 0$ is $\bigl(\sum_{i=1}^{\lfloor u \rfloor} |\Gamma_i| + (u - \lfloor u \rfloor)|\Gamma_{\lfloor u \rfloor + 1}|\bigr)/|\Gamma_0|$ (and $\varphi_\Gamma(u) = u$ for $u \le 0$). Then for every natural number $n$, the image of $G_n$ under the quotient homomorphism $G \to G/H$ equals the lower ramification group of index $\lceil \varphi_H(n) \rceil$ of $G/H$ acting on $R^H$, where $\varphi_H$ is computed for $H$ acting on $R$ and the ceiling is taken in $\mathbb{N}$.
--
--   This is Herbrand's theorem in the lower numbering, $G_nH/H = (G/H)_{\lceil \varphi_H(n)\rceil}$, under the monogenicity hypotheses of Serre's proof (Corps locaux IV §3, Proposition 14 together with Lemma 5). It is the form used to deduce the corresponding statement for extensions of complete discretely valued fields with separable residue field extensions, where monogenicity of the two valuation rings is automatic.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_IsDiscreteValuationRing_map_lowerRamificationGroup_mk_eq_of_adjoin_singleton_eq_top.lean

